---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
	updated="October 13, 2026"
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How OdinPMP collects, uses, and protects information on its website and in the app."
>
	<p>
		This policy explains how Matt Bradford handles information when you visit odinpmp.com,
		join the waitlist, or use the OdinPMP app. Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@odinpmp.com"
			>hello@odinpmp.com</a
		> with privacy questions.
	</p>

	<h2>Information we collect</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Information you provide.</strong> A waitlist entry may include your name, email, company,
			company size, industry, comments, and beta interest. App use may include account details, workspace
			memberships, projects, tasks, comments, files, stakeholder details, bug reports, and support messages.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Sign-in and technical information.</strong> We process information needed to authenticate you,
			including login method, session data, IP address, browser details, timestamps, and service logs.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Connected services.</strong> If you enable a third-party integration, we process the account and
			content needed to provide that connection.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How we use information</h2>
	<p>
		We use this information to run and secure OdinPMP, provide requested features, manage accounts and
		workspaces, respond to support requests, send service messages and invitations, review waitlist entries,
		and improve the product. We do not sell personal information.
	</p>

	<h2>AI and third-party services</h2>
	<p>
		When you use an AI feature, the content needed for that request may be sent to the configured AI
		provider. If your workspace supplies its own provider key, that provider's terms and data practices
		also apply. We use service providers for hosting, email delivery, authentication, and other features
		needed to operate the service. Workspace members may see content according to their access rights.
		We may also disclose information when required by law or to protect the service and its users.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies and website resources</h2>
	<p>
		The app uses cookies and browser storage for sign-in, security, and preferences. The marketing site
		serves its own fonts and loads no third-party resources. It stores your light or dark theme choice in
		your browser. We do not use the marketing site to serve third-party advertising.
	</p>

	<h2>Retention and security</h2>
	<p>
		We keep information while it is needed to provide the service and for legitimate operational or legal
		purposes. When it is no longer needed, we delete or de-identify it, subject to backup and legal
		requirements. We use reasonable measures to protect information, but no online service can promise
		absolute security.
	</p>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<p>
		You can choose what you submit to the waitlist and whether to connect outside services. Workspace
		administrators control access to workspace content. To request access, correction, or deletion of
		personal information, email <a href="mailto:hello@odinpmp.com">hello@odinpmp.com</a>. We will
		respond as required by applicable law and may need to verify your identity first.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this policy as OdinPMP changes. We will post the revised version here with a new
		"Last updated" date. Significant changes may also be communicated through the service or by email.
	</p>
</LegalPage>
